<title>HONG KONG: Nam Fong announces first final results.</title>
<headline>Nam Fong announces first final results.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   50.22</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  76.32 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    526.47</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,574.17</p>
<p>    Company name		 Nam Fong International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 13-20</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   June 20</p>
<p>NOTE - China property group Nam Fong was listed on the Hong Kong stock exchange on December 9, 1996.</p>
<p>On June 27, 1996, the group entered into a provisional sale and purchase agreement to dipose of its entire interest in a wholly-owned subsidiary, Nam Fong Haizhu Plaza Ltd (Haizhu), including the benefit of an unsecured loan due and owing by Haizhu to the group as at June 30, 1996, to an unrelated third party for a total consideration of HK$175 million. The transaction was completed on August 2, 1996 which resulted in profit of HK$76.32 million.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
